Pro is usually the sweet spot: it doubles the cores and quadruples RAM for roughly triple the price, which is where most small production workloads stop being memory-starved. Basic is fine for a single low-traffic site or a dev box; Team only pays off if you're running multiple services or expect real concurrency.

