The pattern across all tiers: the annual commitment always cuts 20% and the two-year term 30%, so the term length matters more than moving up a tier if budget is tight. Enterprise is the only tier where the real choice isn't price but deployment model — pick on-premise only if compliance or data residency actually requires it, since it shifts SLA and ops burden onto you.

